Feature: TC_15_STAFF - AMS Internal Screen E2E Regression Pack

  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Legacy  : "Regression Pack for AMS Internal Screen" (BISSAGL-7295, AT-TC-01 to 03, tmslinks BISSAGL-14750 / 14748 /
  #           14724)
  # Rewritten 15-10-2026 in the StaffSteps vocabulary (the wording the MAPS features run with). One end-to-end
  # scenario; # SECTION markers show where each legacy scenario starts.
  #
  # Purpose:
  #   The read-only AMS screen (Inspections > AMS) for a partnership herd:
  #     - client details (Partnership Farmer, Herd Number) are shown
  #     - each partner herd has its own tab
  #     - the AMS table has every expected column and its pagination works
  #     - the AMS status icons can be hovered
  #
  # Legacy coverage notes carried forward:
  #   - AT-TC-01 first gave agr0191 the AMS, Co-ordination, Processing, Inspections, Risk and Digitising roles through
  #     SSO Administration (agr0043); Section 1 does the same, so the pack does not depend on whatever roles TC_09 or
  #     another run left on agr0191. TC_09 and TC_15 both change agr0191: do not run them at the same time.
  #   - AT-TC-02 repeated the AT-TC-01 checks without the role change; run once here.
  #   - Selenium printed "doesn't exist" for a missing column and carried on; a missing column now fails the step.
  #   - AT-TC-03: the tooltips disappear too quickly to read (legacy note), so the icons are hovered, not asserted.
  #
  # Test data (kept as literals, as in legacy):
  #   Partnership herd IFP10100 / 2024 with partner herds I1330645 and I1020085.
  #   Logins agr0043 (SSO super admin) and agr0191 (the user whose roles change). Password: TD:Password from the
  #   TestData row of this test case, the same for both.
  #
  # Step definitions: stepdefinitions.BISS.STAFF.StaffSteps (SSO Administration, AMS)
  # Author: Aniket Pathare | aniket.pathare@government.ie
  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  @regression @staff @ams @inspections @roles @sso @e2e
  Scenario: AT-STAFF-AMS-E2E-01 - Staff verifies the AMS internal read-only screen for a partnership herd

    # SECTION 1 : Give agr0191 the AMS and processing roles - AT-TC-01 (BISSAGL-14750)
    Given the staff user is logged in to the SSO Administration portal as "agr0043"
    When the staff user replaces the BISS roles of user "agr0191" with the following
      | filter        | role                            |
      | AMS           | BISS AMS 1                      |
      | AMS           | BISS AMS 2                      |
      | CO-ORDINATION | BISS Co-ordination 1            |
      | CO-ORDINATION | BISS Co-ordination 2            |
      | PROCESSING    | BISS Processing 1               |
      | PROCESSING    | BISS Processing 2               |
      | PROCESSING    | BISS Processing 3               |
      | INSPECTIONS   | BISS Inspections 1              |
      | INSPECTIONS   | BISS Inspections 2              |
      | INSPECTIONS   | BISS Inspections 3              |
      | RISK          | BISS Risk Management 1 User     |
      | RISK          | BISS Risk Management 2 User     |
      | RISK          | BISS Risk Management 3 User     |
      | DIGITISING    | BISS Digitising Supervisor User |
      | DIGITISING    | BISS Digitising User            |
    And the staff user signs out of the portal

    # SECTION 2 : Client details, partner herd tabs, columns, pagination - AT-TC-01 / AT-TC-02 (BISSAGL-14750 / 14748)
    Given the staff user is logged in to the BISS internal portal as "agr0191"
    When the staff user opens the AMS screen for herd "IFP10100" for scheme year "2024"
    Then the AMS screen should show the following client details
      | Partnership Farmer |
      | Herd Number        |
    When the staff user switches between the following partner herd tabs
      | I1330645 |
      | I1020085 |
    Then the AMS table should show the following column headers
      | header                    |
      | Townland                  |
      | Parcel no.                |
      | AMS status                |
      | Scheme                    |
      | AMS finding               |
      | AMS monitoring status     |
      | Claimed area (ha)         |
      | Updated claimed area (ha) |
      | Parcel use                |
      | Updated parcel use        |
      | Inspected crop found      |
    And the AMS table pagination should work

    # SECTION 3 : AMS status icons - AT-TC-03 (BISSAGL-14724)
    And the staff user hovers over the following AMS status icons
      | ams-status-yellow |
      | ams-status-green  |
      | ams-status-red    |
      | ams-status-grey   |
